e-masquerade-out-for-blood-is-out?p=1455790#post1455790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You play as a vampire hunter, but the promo promises a possibility of becoming a vampire if you play your cards wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm guessing this is going to be a fail scenario - if the PC dies or turns into a vampire, the game is lost and ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T04:51:46-07:00","id":1456002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455751-vampire-the-masquerade-out-for-blood-is-out?p=1455795#post1455795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm guessing this is going to be a fail scenario - if the PC dies or turns into a vampire, the game is lost and ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having now finished the game:<br /> [Highlight the spoiler]<br /> [<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">No. Becoming a vampire is one of the goals you can pursue. You are not Imbued and you are not a professional vampire hunter. You are just a person in a town that has a vampire in it.</span>]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T04:56:39-07:00","id":1456003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455751-vampire-the-masquerade-out-for-blood-is-out#post1455751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AC/DC; &quot;If you want Blood&quot; plays.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1290350/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Out_for_Blood/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1290350/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Out_for_Blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1290350/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Out_for_Blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://store.steampowered.com/app/1290350/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Out_for_Blood/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I hope it's as good as NIGHT ROAD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thoughts after playing: it's not as good as Night Road, but it's still pretty good. It has fair number of bugs, released with a lot of Faith options dummied out or leading to lame results, and the characters are pretty shallow. But ultimately I had a good time. Solid 6/10 game, gib moar VtM pls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T07:04:08-07:00","id":1456006,"title":"","content":"I'd say 6/10 or maybe 7/10 is fair. It was entertaining, and it's good to have more VtM games. I hope Choice of Games keeps publishing them after Parliament of Knives comes out.<br /> <br /> My spoiler-y thoughts and opinions:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>The human characters could do with fleshing out, but they're fine. The vampires... are morons. In fairness, 5/6 are thinbloods, but I was a better vampire than them <i>before</i> getting embraced.</li> <li>I did enjoy the mystery of trying to work out what I was dealing with, even if I was incredibly disappointed to find out it was just a garden variety Toreador.</li> <li>I find that the most interesting character in the game was the grandfather. Getting more of his story would've been nice.</li> <li>I also feel like the store could have played a bigger part, somehow. I didn't feel like I had a gigantic debt hanging over my head... but maybe that was because I was too busy hunting down a membership card to join the ranks of the undead, so that might be on me.</li> <li>I'm glad getting embraced is an option, but it was so, so hard repressing the urge to murder the only vampire in town who can sire me. <i>So hard</i>.</li> <li>That's not a criticism. Juggling faking being nice to take advantage of someone's usefulness to you vs how badly you just want them to just shuffle the fuck off their immortal coil already is a normal relationship dynamic in vampire society, so it works in the game's favour.</li> <li>Did I feel bad about selling out 3/5 of the thinbloods, all my friends and my humanity? Very. I mean, it didn't <i>stop me</i>, but I felt bad about it.</li> <li>Amanda is an absolute dumbass, and I'm mad at her for several reasons.</li> <li>I was so relieved to discover there's an ending where the Camarilla turn up to clean things up. When you have an entire group in a small town aware of the existence of vampires, you are evidently too incompetent to be trusted with a domain.</li> <li>I spent the game thinking &quot;I know too much, so <i>why am I still alive??</i>&quot;</li> <li>True Faith was way too cheap.</li> <li>I can forgive somebody for being embraced by a Toreador, but I can't forgive being stereotypically boring about it... Or not being a Tzimisce Koldun willing to make me a bride of dracula, or a lab rat, or, hell, furniture or <i>something</i> in exchange for cinematic dark sorcery and the ability to fleshcraft abominations.</li> <li>One of the highlights of the game was having a vampire try to seduce me and getting the option to react by expressing an interest, not out of attraction, but to low-key geek out about fucking a vampire <i>for science!</i></li> <li>I don't know what moron was responsible for the utterly idiotic jackass who broke into my house and made me embarrassed for the necromancers, but I hope they were made an example of. Painfully.</li> <li>I also don't know if it was Perry or Amanda that killed my cat, but it did help me decide to kill them both back on the next run.</li> </ul><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 08-02-2021, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T00:31:10-07:00","id":1456056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455751-vampire-the-masquerade-out-for-blood-is-out?p=1456006#post1456006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><ul><li>I don't know what moron was responsible for the utterly idiotic jackass who broke into my house and made me embarrassed for the necromancers, but I hope they were made an example of. Painfully.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Do you mean Perry? He's not a zombie, he's just a thin-blood with a skin condition. It's one of the possible thin-blood flaws in V5, where they don't heal properly.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> As a whole, I'd say the game did a good job of making me not want to be a vampire. I went through most of the game pursuing path of immortality, and by the end chose to just gun down everyone involved and live a simple life of a store owner.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Amanda isn't a &quot;cool competent lord of the domain&quot;, but I think that's the point and I like the game more for it. She's a rich upstart who has some competent help from Jason and the Circulatory System, but at the end of the day, she's the Prince of Bumfuck Nowhere. Her hold on the city is tenuous even before you start your community watch - she picked a fight with a shop owner and had to tie it on a truce. The mayor is plotting against her (does that magic dirt ever come up again?) and the sheriff just chooses to peace out in the end. As you can point out - all Amanda has going for her is the small-town corruption.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-03T01:35:02-07:00","id":1456057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455751-vampire-the-masquerade-out-for-blood-is-out?p=1456056#post1456056\" rel=\"nofol